# PLAN — OODA-buildbox on zebes: 24/7 .oo-native build/audit rig

File: openOODA/docs/ooda-buildbox.oot

Status: v0.2.0 (2026-10-30), revised after mcode full-scan audit.
Audit board: openOODA/audit/ooda-buildbox_2026_10_30.oot (186 lines).

## 1. Goal

Hermetic container on zebes that builds oodac from source, runs the
audit gate on every change, and fans diffs out to spotlight (ollama) for
multi-engine review — 24/7, unattended. In-box tooling is .oo compiled to
native binaries; HTTP to spotlight uses the proven curl-argv pattern.
No NEW .sh/.py beyond the rules.oot:146-151 carve-outs (P3).

## 2. Decisions (v0.2, revised per mcode)

- D1 (REVISED): no .rs shim. std/net http_client/tls do not emit today and
  oo_tcp_connect is loopback-only (P2), but tui/llm_exec.oo:197 already
  execs curl with explicit argv, TLS, -m 60 timeout, and a 0600 header
  file. ooda-ollama is .oo on that pattern; curl added to the image.
- D2: plan lives in-repo as this .oot (RFC-shaped when promoted); runtime
  queue/results live under /srv/containers/ooda-buildbox, NOT in the
  governed tree (S5 — 256-line cap).
- D3: fast loop = stage1 build + gate per push; fixed-point S1==S2 nightly.
  The fixed point stays oodac/bootstrap/oodac_pure_build (bash) under the
  rules.oot:147 carve-out (C2).

## 3. Image: ooda-buildbox (two-stage)

- v1 builder stage: FROM registry.fedoraproject.org/fedora-toolbox:44
  (same base as rust-buildbox on zebes). Packages: clang, llvm18, git,
  make, curl. No rustc, no nested podman (C11). Fixed-point oodac build
  happens here.
- v2 runtime stage: minimal rootfs assembled from OODA-built static
  binaries (emit/elf backend + oodar_nostd.c freestanding runtime), with
  git and curl as the only external tools, hardened per the rust-buildbox
  profile. Gate: elf backend must pass the full corpus before v2 ships.
  Prereq: std net egress (oo_tcp_connect is loopback-only today) or
  static curl.
- Baked in: oodac bootstrap seed + oodar + std. At container start, verify
  bootstrap/seed/oodac.sha256 against oodac.pub with ed25519_verify_hex and
  fail closed (S6).
- Hardening copied from rust-buildbox/giggle-app units (S1):
  NoNewPrivileges=true, DropCapability=ALL, ReadOnly=true,
  Tmpfs=/tmp:rw,noexec,nosuid,nodev, ProtectSystem=strict,
  ProtectHome=true, PrivateTmp=true, no host PID, volumes :Z.
- Containerfile is the only non-.oo artifact (container DSL).
- Entrypoint: ooda-loop (native .oo binary). No shell entrypoint.

## 4. Layout on zebes (mirrors rust-buildbox: 3 units)

- /etc/containers/systemd/ooda-buildbox.{container,build,network};
  [Build] File= points at the Containerfile dir (C9).
- Network: 10.89.110.0/24. Two planes (C8/S2): internal build plane; a
  filtered egress used ONLY by git fetch and curl to spotlight — never by
  code built from remote content.
- Data: /srv/containers/ooda-buildbox/{queue,cache,repos/<name> per repo}
  (C10 defines per-repo layout and refresh order).
- Logs: /srv/containers/logs/ooda-buildbox.
- Timers: ooda-loop.timer (hourly fast loop), ooda-loop-nightly.timer
  (fixed-point + 20k fuzz + whole-polyrepo recheck).
- Secrets: host Secret= convention; named per consumer, never in the
  queue mount (S7).

## 5. In-box pipeline (all .oo binaries)

1. ooda-loop: git fetch each repo in repos/; record last-seen commit.
2. Stage1 oodac rebuild (BOOTSTRAP_FIXED_POINT=0 via the carve-out script).
3. Gate (real entry points, C1): oodac/qa/suite.oo + openOODA/qa/
   polyrepo_suite.oo + bootstrap/corpus domains + the 2026-10-30 probe
   set (F1-F11) as committed qa probes; double-run determinism filter.
   After ANY compiler change, re-check the whole polyrepo import closure,
   not just the diff (C4 — the F10 class).
4. Fan-out to spotlight via ooda-ollama (.oo + curl argv, -m bounded, C7):
   biggest local model full-scan, mid model adversarial diff, small model
   triage. Model output is ADVISORY (AGENTS.md §7): raw output goes to
   queue/raw/, confirmed findings (verified against source by a second
   engine) to queue/findings.oot with model+prompt-hash+verifier tags
   (S3). A commit turns red only on a source-verified finding.
5. Single-flight via pidfile; all queue writes via file_append_sync only,
   never file_writer_append (C5). Queue integrity: per-file sha256
   manifest verified with ed25519_verify_hex (S4).
6. Gate parses structured `ERR\t<area>\t<detail>` lines; missing
   structured line on expected failure = hard fail (C6).

## 6. Language policy (restated per P3)

- All NEW in-box tooling is .oo. No new .sh/.py; the sanctioned carve-outs
  (rules.oot:146-151: oodac_pure_build, tests/fuzz/test_*.sh, diffrun.sh,
  double_run.sh, lint_oo_size.sh, qa e2e) may be invoked, not extended.
- Prerequisite fixes before the box depends on them: convert the two
  blind sh -c call sites (openOODA/qa/polyrepo_suite.oo:15,21 and
  cli/qa/cmd/probe_dispatch.oo:15) to argv (S10); key the build/emit
  caches by compiler identity like check_cache.oo already does (C3 —
  logged as audit F12 in the oodac board).

## 7. Rollout order

1. F12 (cache keying) + S10 (two sh -c sites) fixed in oodac/openOODA/cli.
2. Containerfile + 3 quadlet units on zebes; boot; seed verify; rebuild.
3. Port the F1-F11 probe set into oodac/qa as committed probes; wire the
   fast loop.
4. ooda-ollama fan-out + timers + queue integrity.
5. Fleet step (257 repos) as its own RFC with rule set + secret-redaction
   pass before any prompt leaves the box (S9).

## 8. Review record

- 2026-10-30: mcode full-scan (spotlight ollama qwen36-35b-uncensored-1m,
  16k ctx) audited v0.1.0 -> board at audit/ooda-buildbox_2026_10_30.oot;
  findings C1-C12, S1-S10, P1-P7, V1-V11 folded into this v0.2.
